  "description": "This course is the foundation of everything else in the Shepherd's Curriculum. Before we can speak rightly about salvation, Scripture, the church, or the Christian life, we must first answer the most fundamental question of all: Who is God? Students will not simply accumulate facts about God. The goal is doxological transformation — that knowing God rightly would produce worship, reverence, and a reordering of life around His glory. As the Puritan Stephen Charnock wrote, meditation on the perfections of God is the greatest purifier of the mind and inflamer of holiness in the heart.",
