          "heading": "6. Summary",
          "html": "<div class=\"detail-table-wrap\"><table class=\"detail-table\"><thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Core Point (from Crossway sources)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Holiness</td><td>Transcendent otherness + moral purity; crown of all attributes (Charnock)</td></tr><tr><td>Isaiah 6</td><td>Holiness → conviction → atonement → commission: the gospel in miniature</td></tr><tr><td>Omniscience</td><td>God knows all things in an eternal instant; His foreknowledge rests on His foreordination (Jones)</td></tr><tr><td>Omnipotence</td><td>Infinite power united with sovereign dominion and perfect goodness (Charnock/Jones)</td></tr><tr><td>Omnipresence</td><td>God fills all things <em>repletively</em> — fully present everywhere, contained nowhere (Charnock)</td></tr><tr><td>Immutability</td><td>God does not change; anchor of every covenant promise (Charnock/DeYoung)</td></tr><tr><td>Eternality</td><td>God exists above and outside time; He governs history, He does not react to it (Charnock)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>## 📚 EXTRA READING — Personal Library</p>\n<p><strong>Assigned for this session:</strong></p>\n<ul><li><em>The Holiness of God</em> — R.C. Sproul, Chapters 1–4</li><li><em>None Greater</em> — Matthew Barrett, Chapter 3: \"A God Without Limits\"</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Reflection prompt:</strong> Which of God's incommunicable attributes covered in this session do you find hardest to hold onto in daily life? Write a short, honest prayer wrestling with it.</p>\n<p><strong>Memory verse:</strong> Revelation 4:8 — <em>\"Holy, holy, holy, is the Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come!\"</em></p>\n<p>## 🔬 LAB / RESEARCH</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Worship Song Analysis:</strong> Choose a contemporary worship song popular in Philippine youth ministry. Does it reflect God's holiness and transcendence, or primarily His accessibility and friendship? What, if anything, is missing? Write a 200-word critique using concepts from this session.</li></ol>\n<ol><li><strong>Attribute Map:</strong> On a single page, draw God at the centre and map at least 8 attributes around Him. For each, write a one-sentence definition and one supporting Scripture verse.</li></ol>\n<ol><li><strong>Group Discussion:</strong> <em>\"Why does the holiness of God feel uncomfortable or irrelevant in today's church culture? What would it look like for your church to recover a robust sense of God's greatness in worship?\"</em></li></ol>",
          "plainText": "| Attribute | Core Point (from Crossway sources) |\n|-----------|----------------------------------|\n| Holiness | Transcendent otherness + moral purity; crown of all attributes (Charnock) |\n| Isaiah 6 | Holiness → conviction → atonement → commission: the gospel in miniature |\n| Omniscience | God knows all things in an eternal instant; His foreknowledge rests on His foreordination (Jones) |\n| Omnipotence | Infinite power united with sovereign dominion and perfect goodness (Charnock/Jones) |\n| Omnipresence | God fills all things repletively — fully present everywhere, contained nowhere (Charnock) |\n| Immutability | God does not change; anchor of every covenant promise (Charnock/DeYoung) |\n| Eternality | God exists above and outside time; He governs history, He does not react to it (Charnock) |\n\n\n## 📚 EXTRA READING — Personal Library\n\nAssigned for this session:\n- The Holiness of God — R.C. Sproul, Chapters 1–4\n- None Greater — Matthew Barrett, Chapter 3: \"A God Without Limits\"\n\nReflection prompt: Which of God's incommunicable attributes covered in this session do you find hardest to hold onto in daily life? Write a short, honest prayer wrestling with it.\n\nMemory verse: Revelation 4:8 — \"Holy, holy, holy, is the Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come!\"\n\n\n## 🔬 LAB / RESEARCH\n\n1. Worship Song Analysis: Choose a contemporary worship song popular in Philippine youth ministry. Does it reflect God's holiness and transcendence, or primarily His accessibility and friendship? What, if anything, is missing? Write a 200-word critique using concepts from this session.\n\n2. Attribute Map: On a single page, draw God at the centre and map at least 8 attributes around Him. For each, write a one-sentence definition and one supporting Scripture verse.\n\n3. Group Discussion: *\"Why does the holiness of God feel uncomfortable or irrelevant in today's church culture? What would it look like for your church to recover a robust sense of God's greatness in worship?\""
